    "description": "The so-called House of the Drinking Contest is a third-century C.E. townhouse located at Seleucia Pieria.",
    "details": "<p>The house was excavated during the 1930s in a campaign supported by Princeton University, the Louvre, the Baltimore Museum of Art, and the Worcester Art Museum. Some of the mosaics from the site were dispersed to global museums.</p>",
